@@ -18,3 +18,12 @@ first. The discount comes off the order's items only, never its shipping, and th
 
 An unknown code, or `WELCOME5` on a smaller order, is refused with an error saying why, and the order keeps the code it
 had. Whether an order ships free is decided on its items before any discount.
+
+## Monthly export
+
+`orders.exportMonth(month)` gives the accountant's spreadsheet the orders placed in a month, as CSV text. `month` is
+`YYYY-MM`; a month that is not is refused. The text has a header line, `order,date,customer,total`, then one line per
+order placed in that month (its date as the order stores it), by order number. `total` is what the customer pays, in
+euros with two decimals, so a discount is already taken off. The export carries no customer email addresses or phone
+numbers. A value with a comma, a quote or a line break is quoted, with its quotes doubled. A month with no orders gives
+the header line alone. Each line ends with a line feed.
